// Seven equal bars on 1:2, the proportion of the designer's 2800 by 1400 pixel image.
// The middle bar is a gradient along the fly, from the edge color at both ends to the center color.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Quoigenic flag"
  designer "Selenelion Aberration"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  series "quoigenic-flag"
  version "normal"
  source "https://selenated.com/flags/quoigenic"
  source "https://cdn.selenated.com/img/a065.png"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20260107142744/https://pluralpedia.org/w/Quoigenic"
  note "The designer's own flag page, on The Aberration's site selenated.com, read on 13 November 2026, defines quoigenic as often meaning that a system doesn't know, doesn't care or is mixed in terms of origin. It gives the meanings: orange, recognition of quoigenic systems; middle orange, support for quoigenic systems in general; light orange, understanding that quoigenic doesn't just mean mixed origins; middle stripe, the diversity of the system experience and of the meanings of quoigenic; light teal, understanding that quoigenic systems can technically fall into endogenic or traumagenic categories but prefer this label; middle teal, support for quoigenic systems influenced by or created due to trauma; teal, recognition of quoigenics who haven't been through trauma or became systems for other reasons. Pluralpedia credits the flag to Selenelion Aberration. The page isn't dated, and no date is given."
  note "The page describes this 'normal' version as seven stripes, three shades of orange darkening toward the top and three of teal darkening toward the bottom, with a middle stripe that is 'a center-meeting gradient of orange and teal'. The colors are read from its image, 2800 by 1400 pixels with stripes of exactly 200: #ffb354, #ffcc61, #ffde98, then the gradient, then #79b3b7, #579dab and #397d93. The gradient changes only along the fly, from #faddac at both edges to #b3ddd7 at the center, evenly, with slight dithering. The page gives no hex values."
  note "The page also has a simplified version, five stripes with white in the middle, which isn't encoded here. The designer's traumagenic flag (traumagenic) has the same construction."
}
palette {
  orange "#ffb354"
  middle-orange "#ffcc61"
  light-orange "#ffde98"
  edge "#faddac"
  center "#b3ddd7"
  light-teal "#79b3b7"
  middle-teal "#579dab"
  teal "#397d93"
  middle gradient edge center edge
}
proportion hoist=1 fly=2

bars orange middle-orange light-orange middle light-teal middle-teal teal
